W: 1. Farewell to old England for ever,
W: Farewell to my old pals as well,
W: Farewell to the well-known Old Bailey
W: Where I once used to look such a swell.
W:
W: (Chorus:)
W: Singing too-ral, li-oo-ral li-ad-di-ty,
W: Singing too-ral, li-oo-ral, li-ay,
W: Singing too-ral, li-oo-ral, li-ad-di-ty,
W: For we're bound for the Botany Bay.
W:
W: 2. There's the captain as is our commander,
W: There's the bosun and all the ship's crew,
W: There's the first and the second class passengers,
W: Knows what we poor convicts go through.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 3. 'Taint leaving old England we cares about,
W: 'Yaint 'cos we mis-spells wot we knows,
W: But becos all we light-fingered gentry
W: Hops around with a log on our toes.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. Oh, had I the wings of a turtle-dove
W: I'd soar on my pinions so high,
W: Slap bang to the arms of my Polly love,
W: And in her sweet presence I'd die.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 5. Now all my young Dookies and Duchesses,
W: Take warning from what I've to say,
W: Mind all is your own that you touchesses
W: Or you'll find us in Botany Bay.
W: (Chorus)
